#
# Load commands for the PCIscan kernel server.
#
# The scan runs as part of the load sequence: CALL invokes pciScanEntry
# during initialization, so no DriverKit device matching and no Mach
# port traffic are involved. Results go out through IOLog; the userland
# front end (pcils) harvests them from the system log.
#
# START is required because this server listens on no ports - without it
# kern_loader would wait for a message that never comes.
#
CALL pciScanEntry 0
WIRE
START
